-- title:
--   Selected roots have their prescribed prime-power order
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge0$, let $q_i$ be nonzero natural numbers for $i<d$, and set $A=\prod_{i<d}\mathbb Z/q_i$. A primary coordinate for a prime $p$ is an index with $p\mid q_i$. For supports in $A$, write $Q_S$ for ordered-sum counts, $P_\chi(S)=\sum_{x\in S}\chi(x)$, and $\mathcal O_B(S)=(Q_S,(P_{\chi_i}(S))_i)$ for a character bank $B$. For typed square entries $E$ on $A$ and any selected-bank index $i$, $$\zeta_i\text{ is primitive of order }p_i^{k_i+1}.$$
--
--   The root, prime and depth are those of the entries-selected bank.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/RecohSelectedDecoder.lean, lines 135–142; source file SHA-256 9df6959d546259a3037e3c1d20bf5d4697a947811925e34ec7c4b4ec93c577b0; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.recoh_selected_bank_root_primitive

